  "instance_name": "peanut_stereotype",
  "label": "Peanut Stereotype",
  "description": "The phrase 'eating peanuts' is used to imply that Mexicans are subsisting on low-quality, meager food, reinforcing the idea that they are impoverished and inferior. This is a derogatory stereotype that reduces their diet and lifestyle to something crude and unrefined, further dehumanizing them. It is often paired with 'starving' to emphasize their supposed lack of resources.",
